    V+  ## Appendix A — Proofs
    V+  Nine proofs are given in full in the chapters and are cross-referenced here. The remaining ten are written out below — nineteen in all.
    V+  ### A.3 Projections of closed sets are closed
    V+  ### A.8 The total-order criterion at d = 2
    V+  x ∨ y = (uⱼ, max(b₁,b₂)), and max(b₁,b₂) ∈ F(uⱼ)
    V+  x ∧ y = (uᵢ, min(b₁,b₂)), and min(b₁,b₂) ∈ F(uᵢ)
    V+  ### A.9 μΛ in closed form
    V+  Proof. Under the Birkhoff isomorphism, the interval [x,y] in Λ is isomorphic to J(Q), the lattice of
    V+  down-sets of the induced subposet on Q = y∖x. If Q is an antichain, J(Q) is the Boolean lattice 2^{|Q|} and
    V+  μ(∅,Q) = (−1)^{|Q|}. If Q is not an antichain, the atoms of J(Q) are the singletons {m} for m minimal in Q,
    V+  and their join is the down-set of the minimal elements, which is a proper subset of Q because some element
    V+  of Q lies strictly above a minimal one. By the crosscut theorem (Rota 1964, Cor. to Thm 3), μ(∅,Q) vanishes
    V+  whenever the join of the atoms is not the top. ∎
    V+  ### A.10 The tree factorisation of the void count
    P+  # APPENDICES
    P+  # Appendix A — Proofs
    P+  Ten proofs are given in full in the chapters and are cross-referenced here. The remaining seven are written out below — seventeen in all.
    P+  A.3 Projections of closed sets are closed
    P+  A.8 The total-order criterion at d = 2
    P+  x ∨ y = (uⱼ, max(b₁,b₂)), and max(b₁,b₂) ∈ F(uⱼ) x ∧ y = (uᵢ, min(b₁,b₂)), and min(b₁,b₂) ∈ F(uᵢ)
    P+  A.9 μΛ in closed form
    P+  Proof. Under the Birkhoff isomorphism, the interval [x,y] in Λ is isomorphic to the lattice of down-sets of
    P+  the induced subposet on Q = y∖x. The Möbius function of J(Q) is (−1)^{|Q|} when Q is an antichain — in
    P+  which case J(Q) is the Boolean lattice 2^{|Q|} — and vanishes otherwise, since a non-antichain interval
    P+  decomposes as a direct product with a chain factor of length ≥ 2, whose Möbius function is zero above its
    P+  atom. ∎
    P+  A.10 The tree factorisation of the void count
    P+  #{2S} = max(0, min(hi₇, k) − lo₇ + 1) #{g} = max(0, min(hi₆, q, 2(2f+1)) − lo₆ + 1)

